export
Usage: export NAME=VALUE  |  export NAME

Mark a variable so child processes inherit it.

A shell builtin. Without export a variable exists only inside the shell
itself.

	export TERM=linux
	export PATH="$PATH:/opt/bin"
	export		list everything currently exported

xos's init exports HOME, TERM and the XDG_* paths this way before it
hands you a shell.

See also: set, unset, read
